Okay, so the map from the vending machine as well as the help map command
will now show your current location in ansi if you are inside eternal city.  
Maps containing ansi are generated ahead of time, stored in files, and served
when a player needs them.  If you want to change the contents of the map, you
have to manually regenerate the files, which is outlined below.  Here's how 
it works:

Setting up the rooms to be mapped:

Each room we want to represent on the map can have a couple of variables 
set( ) in them.

map_symbol:  a string representing what symbol to use on the map for this 
             room.  If a room does not have a map_symbol set, none of its 
             exits will be traversed and it will not get drawn on the map.  
             Maps with a symbol of '?' will not have an ansi map file 
             generated for them.  
map_hint_x:
map_hint_y:  integer rendering hints for how to draw the symbol for this room.
             by default the map will print room symbols starting at their
             location in the map.  For single character symbols, this isn't
             a problem.  But if we want the symbol to be multiple characters
             we might want to adjust the way the symbol is drawn.  
             For example, Dave's Throne Room is drawn with the symbol DTR.
             By default the room would show up on the map as:
             
                                    |
                                    DTR
             
             This is slightly ugly, so we set a map_hint_x value of -1 in the
             room, which tells the generator to move the x coordinate of this
             room one space to the left.  The room is now drawn as:
             
                                    |
                                   DTR
                          
map_units:   a mapping that indicates how many units away a particular exit 
             in the room is from its destination.  Eternal city was not
             designed in a perfect grid, so the map has to use some tricks
             to display itself properly.  It is very important to set the
             map_units in all rooms that have irregular units.  If you set
             the 'west' units in one room as 2, but do not set the 'east
             units in the destination room, you're not guarenteed that the
             units will be recognized when generating the map.  If an exit 
             does not have a value in the map_units mapping, or the 
             mapping is not set, a standard distance of 1 is assumed.
            
map_extras:  a mapping containg information about spots on the map that 
             would normally be dropped when processing rooms.  The generator
             stays within rooms that are in the same cabal, so if you want
             rooms outside your cabal to be added to the map, you need to
             use this mapping.  It's format is:
             
                 ([ direction : ({ symbol, map_hint_x, map_hint_y }) ])
                 
             The direction is the exit from this room that we want to use
             on the map.  The values are the same as for regular map rooms.
                           
How to generate new maps:

Generating new maps is done in two steps.  The first step is to generate the
structure we're going to use for making all our maps.  This is done by calling
the function start_travel_room( ) in the generator.  It takes a little while to
build the data structure, but when it is completed the map it intends to 
generate will be displayed on your screen.  You can also display the default
map by calling the function print_generic_map( ).  

Once all the rooms have been traversed and you have verified that the map
generated is the one you want to use, it is time to build all the ansi maps.
This is done by calling generate_map_files( ).  Again, this takes some time
to complete, but when the generator will display the generic map to signal
completion.  

Issues and Limitations:

Right now the generator only lets cabal members call the functions that 
generate the maps.

The map width and height must be defined so it has an extra space on all 
sides of whatever the maximum possible map size is.  

The map generator only understands how to travel in the 4 major compass
directions north, south, east and west. 

